      "writtenOn": "2023-11-27T15:07:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this will trigger an assert with the approx-fit textures because `Device::Make` passes in the instantiated target with the larger binned dimensions, and the original `ii.dimensions()` for the device size.\n\nBut in `DrawContext::Make` it asserts that the device size has to match the texture if the texture is instantiated. I think we need to adjust the check to let it be a larger texture (and then make sure that the DrawPasses use the deviceSize as the viewport, which I think is already the case for the non-instantiated deferred targets).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 95
      },
      "revId": "e76f9b97f01b93a8580448afb02ae16604618e88",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "acb6de67_0dc4365a",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Device.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 274,
      "author": {
        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-27T19:53:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it make sense to just leave the viewport, and normalized fragment coordinates, in backing-target space? The scissor we do define based on deviceSize, in DrawPass (the viewport is currently always set to the target dimensions, in RenderPassTask).\n\nI also changed the related isInstantiated() checks in DrawContext::Make and DrawPass::Make to isFullyLazy(), following up on discussion way back in http://review.skia.org/596357. This way we check dimensions of non-instantiated, non-fully-lazy targets as well.",
      "parentUuid": "71f58050_538792a4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 95
      },
      "revId": "e76f9b97f01b93a8580448afb02ae16604618e88",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "88655225_94a4c003",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Device.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 274,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-28T02:04:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In Ganesh I believe we handled the viewport and NDC space as the full backing size. For now as long as we\u0027re setting the scissor, I think we will draw fine.\n\nHaving the NDC space and viewport connected back to the device size may be useful to avoid flakiness in rendering where MSAA sampling or coverage interpolation changes slightly due to rasterization differences resulting from normalizing with a different denominator (full target vs. the deviceSize). If we can plumb it through later on, it\u0027s probably worth making the NDC mapping consistent so we should get the same rasterization behavior regardless of approx or exact-fit backing textures. But I think that can be a separate CL and we just file a bug.",
      "parentUuid": "acb6de67_0dc4365a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 95
      },
      "revId": "e76f9b97f01b93a8580448afb02ae16604618e88",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
